[
  {
    "sha": "42ee5e383b18249049e1dbf1a607ee0a4838defb",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDQyZWU1ZTM4M2IxODI0OTA0OWUxZGJmMWE2MDdlZTBhNDgzOGRlZmI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T04:25:00Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T04:25:00Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): microlift pieces take longer chords only where they leave no sliver\n\nThe microlift acceptance (adaptive/lift.rs, lift_returns) compared the\nlifted plan's worst reading with the spiral's and flipped on nanometres:\non the 60 x 14 slot 10 of 30 sub-micron twins read 48.0 or 48.5 deg\nagainst 47.5 and dropped the lifted plan (the bare spiral then fails the\ntravel law and the slot falls to Offset rings).\n\nThe reading was not a rounding tie. A piece re-thinned to longer chords\n(0.01 mm sag) cuts inside the arc it replaces and leaves a sliver on the\nstock side; the next piece meets it as one or two rim samples the spiral\nnever planned, and which cell centres the sliver covers is chance.\n\nA piece now takes its longer chords only where the planner's stock shows\nthey change nothing: they read within the bound and leave standing no\ncell the piece's own chords clear (lift_coarse::cut, Raster::stands_over).\nThe acceptance keeps its law with no tolerance (lift::keeps): a lifted\nplan reading over the spiral, or over the bound where the spiral read\nunder it, is never kept. 30 of 30 slot twins now keep the lifted plan,\neach reading its worst where the spiral does.\n\nrotary_adaptive's r6.2 neck levels (5.7, 5.2) were pinned refused for\ntravel on the same coin (on main one or the other is HSM-planned with\nthe openings 16, 62, 250 or 510 nm deeper); they are now HSM-planned on\nmicrolift returns and pinned so, their dexel load (20.3 % D at the bore\nexit) and radius 5.2's three 5.1-5.5 deg breaks pinned as read (#1050).\n\ncoarsen moves to lift_coarse.rs with the new test (lift.rs stays under\nthe 400-line law). Decision: docs/decisions/982-microlift-acceptance.md.\n\nFixes #982\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
